.TH LIANLI-CONTROL 1 "" "Lian Li Linux"
.SH NAME
lianli-control \- inspect installation and coordinate daemon services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lianli-control
.I COMMAND
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This helper provides installation diagnostics and constrained service operations.
Use the GUI for normal mode switching, settings migration and recovery.
Internal worker commands are implementation interfaces, not general-purpose
administration commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B diagnose
Inspect service setup without starting a daemon or accessing hardware.
.TP
.B diagnose-runtime \-\-hid-backend hidraw|rusb
Inspect the executing account's credentials, host lock and USB node permissions
without device I/O. The default backend is hidraw. A successful permission check
does not prove that a device driver can open or operate the hardware.
.TP
.B distrobox-service-unit
Print a host user hardware-daemon unit without installing or starting it.
Use \-\-desktop-session for the separate capture unit, \-\-box NAME to select the
box, \-\-distrobox-enter PATH for the host executable and \-\-binaries DIRECTORY for
the installed guest binaries. Default paths are /usr/bin/distrobox-enter and
/usr/bin. Review and install the generated unit on the host.
Use \-\-system-uid UID with \-\-system-config PATH to print a system-manager
recipe running as the box owner with separate guest settings. Automatic setup
and migration for that recipe are still being integrated. Do not enable it
until the coordinated host setup is available.
.TP
.B inspect-state \-\-config PATH \-\-working-directory DIRECTORY
Inspect saved configuration, profiles, templates and media references.
Add \-\-check-assets to open referenced assets under the executing account,
including inactive profiles and templates. This does not change settings or
prove access under a different daemon account or filesystem namespace.
.TP
.B check-destination \-\-scope user|system
Authorize and preflight a native service destination without stopping the current daemon.
.TP
.B select-mode \-\-scope user|system
Administrator-only selection of one native hardware mode while all daemons are
stopped. User mode requires \-\-user-uid UID; system mode uses the packaged lianli
account. This low-level selection does not perform settings migration or enable
and start the destination service. Prefer the GUI's coordinated switch.
.TP
.B stop-service \-\-invocation-id ID [\-\-scope user|system]
Stop only the daemon belonging to the specified host service mode and invocation.
The default scope is user. The caller must own the daemon process.
This command is used by generated Distrobox units.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \-\-help for command-specific options and \-\-version for the application version.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/lianli/service-selection.json
records the selected account/mode or an unfinished switch gate. Do not delete it
to bypass service ownership checks; use recovery for an interrupted switch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lianli-daemon (1),
.BR lianli-gui (1),
.BR lianli-session (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sgtaziz/lian-li-linux/tree/main/docs
